"About 300 original skills were designed by Artonans who believed they were saving existence."
"All survive in some System version, guarded by their designers' philosophical descendants."
"Original skills follow ancient design tastes, so they look poorly made to modern summoners."
"Nothing labels a skill as original, even on a summoner's display."
"Original skills have no maximum level."
"Holders may be offered the next step on the original progression path instead of new skills."
"Let Me Take Your Luggage is original skill number 112, hidden under a shroud of mediocrity."
"The originals had names of their own, many hard to render poetically."
"The System sometimes offers an S-rank a brand-new, one-of-a-kind path after they accept a class."
"Such offers carry extra sparkle, but also risk; option lists hold traps as well as treasures."
"Instructors advise against affixing undiscovered options: 'Why be the first through the gate?'"
